 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon GameLift API (2015-10-01). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Aliases, custom locations, game session queues and FlexMatch rule sets are configuration metadata: no build, script, fleet, container group, compute, game server, game session, player session, placement or matchmaking ticket exists. CreateFleet, CreateGameSession, StartGameSessionPlacement, StartMatchmaking and the other hosting and session APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Aliases support only TERMINAL routing because no fleet exists; alias identifiers are alias- followed by 32 hexadecimal digits. Game session queues refuse destinations, and notification targets and allowed locations are stored without contacting Amazon SNS or checking locations. ListAliases RoutingStrategyType and ListLocations Filters are refused, and ListLocations lists only custom locations, not AWS Regions or Local Zones. Rule set bodies must be JSON objects with ruleLanguageVersion and teams; no further FlexMatch validation is performed and rule sets cannot be updated, as in the official API. Matchmaking configurations and ValidateMatchmakingRuleSet return HTTP 501.",
  "title": "Amazon GameLift Servers (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2015-10-01"
 },
 "openapi": "3.1.0",
